      "text": "The factor is the average of the two low-prior-return (loser) portfolios minus the average of the two high-prior-return (winner) portfolios, across small and big stocks:\n\nLT_Rev = 0.5 \u00d7 (Small LoPRIOR + Big LoPRIOR) \u2212 0.5 \u00d7 (Small HiPRIOR + Big HiPRIOR)\n\nThe file contains several sections (value-weighted, equal-weighted, counts, sizes), so the script reads only the first monthly value-weighted block. Missing-value codes (-99.99, -999) become NaN, and months lacking any of the six portfolio returns are dropped.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef parse_value(tok):\n    tok = tok.strip()\n    try:\n        v = float(tok)\n    except ValueError:\n        return np.nan\n    if abs(v + 99.99) < 1e-6 or abs(v + 999.0) < 1e-6:\n        return np.nan\n    return v\n\n\ndef main():\n    fname = \"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_60_13.csv\"\n    with open(fname, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        lines = f.readlines()\n\n    rows = []\n    started = False\n    for line in lines:\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.strip().split(\",\")]\n        if len(parts) == 7 and re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{6}\", parts[0]):\n            rows.append([int(parts[0])] + [parse_value(p) for p in parts[1:]])\n            started = True\n        elif started:\n            # first monthly value-weighted block has ended\n            break\n\n    cols = [\"date\", \"SL\", \"SM\", \"SH\", \"BL\", \"BM\", \"BH\"]\n    df = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=cols)\n\n    # Long-term reversal: losers (LoPRIOR) minus winners (HiPRIOR), averaged over size\n    lt = 0.5 * (df[\"SL\"] + df[\"BL\"]) - 0.5 * (df[\"SH\"] + df[\"BH\"])\n\n    out = pd.DataFrame({\"date\": df[\"date\"].astype(int), \"value\": lt})\n    out = out.dropna().reset_index(drop=True)\n    out[\"date\"] = out[\"date\"].astype(int)\n\n    out.to_csv(\"output.csv\", index=False, columns=[\"date\", \"value\"])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
